    "result": {
      "ok": true,
      "stdout": "Orchestrate MG runtime data strictly from the package\r\nruntime_data_acquisition_recipe.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --package TEXT REQUIRED           Hydrated MG package path (local:// or absolute).\r\n      --target-material-id TEXT         Target video material id.\r\n      --target-seg-id TEXT              Target segment id (apply window).\r\n      --output-dir TEXT REQUIRED        Directory for runtime data files and manifest.\r\n      --recipe-json TEXT                Optional runtime_data_acquisition_recipe override (JSON, file, or\r\n                                        @file); package recipe is the default.\r\n      --materials-xml TEXT              Optional current Materials XML for runtime_input context.\r\n      --runtime-target-json TEXT        Optional runtime_target JSON\r\n                                        (description/object_desc/plane_desc/seed_time_ms).\r\n      --ref TEXT                        Draft ref used as source context by studio/stylecut. Subject\r\n                                        providers resolve the source video from it; plane providers may\r\n                                        use the active draft session.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track-subject-mask / encode-subject-alpha / track-plane-quad are the atomic steps it dispatches; they can also be called directly.\r\n\r\nNOTE\r\n  Produces subject_alpha.v1 / subject_transform.v1 / plane_quad.v1 with time_base=draft_us (frame time_us rebased to 0). Apply via `draft effect add --type motiongraph --runtime-data-manifest <manifest>`.\r\n",
      "stderr": "",
      "output": "Orchestrate MG runtime data strictly from the package\r\nruntime_data_acquisition_recipe.\r\n\r\nAGENT QUICKSTART (driving this as an agent? start here):\r\n  Browse commands:  lyra-cli <domain> --help\r\n\r\nUSAGE:\r\n  lyra-cli <domain> <[subdomain] ...> <action> [--flags] [--options]\r\n\r\n\r\nOPTIONS:\r\n  -h, --help                            Print this help message and exit\r\n      --package TEXT REQUIRED           Hydrated MG package path (local:// or absolute).\r\n      --target-material-id TEXT         Target video material id.\r\n      --target-seg-id TEXT              Target segment id (apply window).\r\n      --output-dir TEXT REQUIRED        Directory for runtime data files and manifest.\r\n      --recipe-json TEXT                Optional runtime_data_acquisition_recipe override (JSON, file, or\r\n                                        @file); package recipe is the default.\r\n      --materials-xml TEXT              Optional current Materials XML for runtime_input context.\r\n      --runtime-target-json TEXT        Optional runtime_target JSON\r\n                                        (description/object_desc/plane_desc/seed_time_ms).\r\n      --ref TEXT                        Draft ref used as source context by studio/stylecut. Subject\r\n                                        providers resolve the source video from it; plane providers may\r\n                                        use the active draft session.\r\n      --channel <online|test|local_test> \r\n                                        Material request channel. Use `test` or `local_test` for internal\r\n                                        test resources.\r\n  -v, --version                         Show version information and exit.\r\n      --jq TEXT                         Pretty-print JSON output; with an optional selector like\r\n                                        .result.items[0].id, output the selected JSON value instead of\r\n                                        the full schema envelope.\r\n\r\nWORKFLOW\r\n  build-runtime-manifest  strictly resolves package recipe steps into a standard runtime_data_manifest.\r\n  track-subject-mask / encode-subject-alpha / track-plane-quad are the atomic steps it dispatches; they can also be called directly.\r\n\r\nNOTE\r\n  Produces subject_alpha.v1 / subject_transform.v1 / plane_quad.v1 with time_base=draft_us (frame time_us rebased to 0). Apply via `draft effect add --type motiongraph --runtime-data-manifest <manifest>`.\r\n",
